{
  "dom_id": "step-q70262",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality ${x}^{2}-8>0$ using the absolute value method.",
  "worked_solution": "Bringing the constant term to the right-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8 & >0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & >8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the square root of both sides of the inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & >8 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & >\\sqrt{8} \\\\ |x| & >2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the definition of absolute value, we must have\n\n$$\nx<-2\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{or}\\,x>2\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nThe solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-2\\sqrt{2})\\cup (2\\sqrt{2},\\infty ).$",
